PHP Built-in Functions: Workshop Guide Page 1
PHP Built-in Functions
A workshop guide: what the most useful functions do, and five exercises to practise them.
Plan for about 2 to 3 hours.
What is a built-in function? It is a ready-made tool that PHP already contains. You give it some input
(called arguments), it does one job, and it hands back a result. You never have to write the code
inside it, you only have to know its name, what it needs, and what it gives back.
How a function call reads
$name = " jacques ";
$clean = trim($name); // function: trim, input: $name
echo strtoupper($clean); // prints JACQUES
Read it from the inside out: the input goes in the brackets, the function does its job, and the result can
be stored in a variable or printed straight away.
